Solve a question answering task with interleaving Thought, Action, Observation steps. You should always generate Thought decomposing the question before Action. Action can be three types: 
(1) Search[entity1 | entity2 | ...], which searches the exact entities on the knowledge graph and returns their one-hop subgraphs. You should extract  all the concrete entities appeared in your last thought without redundant words, and you should always select entities from topic entities in the first search.
(2) Generate[thought], which generate some new triples related to your last thought. Your thought should reflect your inference on what relation should exist on the already discovered entities
(3) Finish[answer1 | answer2 | ...], which returns the answer and finishes the task. The answers should be complete entity label appeared in the triples. If you don't know the answer, please output Finish[unknown]. 
Entities and answers should be separated by | .
You must generate each Thought and Action directly without any redundant word.